Instructions for use: program [-option value]
[option]
1. log output mode:
    -printf [bool]:	enable/disable printf interface
    -syslog [bool]:	enable/disable syslog/dbgview interface
    -file [bool]:	enable/disable log write in file
2. log level control:
    -leveldbg [bool]:	enable/disable debug level log output
    -levelinfo [bool]:	enable/disable info level log output
    -levelwarn [bool]:	enable/disable warning level log output
    -levelerror [bool]:	enable/disable error level log output
    -levelfatal [bool]:	enable/disable fatal level log output
3. log output property:
	-focus [string]:by highlighting the focus of the module log output is displayed the color of the parameter false to turn off
    -time [bool]:	enable/disable increase date time prefix
    -tid [bool]:	enable/disable increase thread id prefix
    -logpath [string]:	edit log file path, switch files when the current date changes
    -console:		redirect printf to console, linux platform only
    -tty [string]:	redirect printf to terminal, linux platform only, if there is no value, redirect to the current terminal
    -show [string]:	show module state debug information, use '-show zdebug attribute' output zdebug attribute
[value]
    [ bool ]:		enable: true 1, disable: false 0
    [ integer ]:	number
    [ string ]:		text
[example]
    program -file true
    program -leveldbg
    program [-tty] or [-tty /dev/pts/3]
    program -show zdebug attribute